# A program's own PascalCase folder is a module folder (docs/module-model-options.md option B),
# as in lib/ and packages: Hud/ and its camelCase subfolder parts/ are ONE module `Hud`, its files
# call each other with no import, and like every program file it needs no import here (bare or
# `Hud.` qualified). The PascalCase folder Hud/Minimap/ is a module of its own (`Minimap.`).
# camelCase folders still only break a tie: `enemies.tick()`, `particles.tick()`.
func main() {
  log(Hud.title())
  log(drawHud())
  log("minimap zoom {Minimap.zoom()}")
  log("enemies {enemies.tick()} particles {particles.tick()}")
}
